  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Unsettled weather and cooler temperatures through \nthe weekend.\n\nUpper level trough and associated closed low over the central Great \nLakes will move northeast across the region through Saturday night. \nA surface low over southern Ontario will continue to progress east \nsending a cold front across the area through this afternoon. A few \nshowers will continue across the region as the front moves through. \nOnce the front moves through, a cool moist air mass will wrap around \nto support lake enhanced showers downwind of the lakes tonight and \nSaturday. \n\nAnother upper level trough will drop southeast across the upper and \ncentral Great Lakes Sunday supporting a surface low moving through \nnorthern Ontario and Quebec, where a pair of fronts approach the \nregion Sunday and Sunday night. Ahead of the fronts, lake enhanced \nshowers will persist east of both lakes during the day on Sunday \nbefore more widespread precipitation arrives Sunday night.",
